  "title": "Kirby Problem 3.66",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Suppose that $Y$ is a closed, oriented 3-manifold, and let $S_{2,\\infty}(Y)$ denote the Kauffman bracket skein module over $R=\\mathbb{Z}[A,A^{-1}]$ as in Problem 3.65.\n\n(a) Is the dimension\n\n$$\n\\dim_{\\mathbb{Q}(A)} S_{2,\\infty}(Y)\\otimes_R \\mathbb{Q}(A)\n$$\n\nequal to the dimension of the degree 0 part of Abouzaid--Manolescu's sheaf-theoretic Floer homology $HP^{\\bullet}_{\\#}(Y)$ from [AM20]?\n\n(b) When is $S_{2,\\infty}(Y)\\otimes_R\\mathbb{Q}[A,A^{-1}]$ tame, as defined in Problem 3.65?",
